" Spec [Tablature][[Editing]] 1 (`||`, songwriter#tab#Lint): align bar pipes
" across all strings and normalise dashes so that the first note of a bar sits
" two dashes after the left pipe and the last note two dashes before the right
" pipe. Note order is preserved.

Given (does not lint non-tab lines):
  some prose
  another line

Execute (does not lint non-tab lines):
  call cursor(1, 1)
  call songwriter#tab#Lint()
Expect:
  some prose
  another line

Given (an empty bar (no notes) becomes exactly two dashes):
  e|---------|

Execute (an empty bar (no notes) becomes exactly two dashes):
  call cursor(1, 1)
  call songwriter#tab#Lint()
Expect:
  e|--|

Given (a line without a closing pipe keeps its notes, its bar is closed):
  e|--3--5--

Execute (a line without a closing pipe keeps its notes, its bar is closed):
  call cursor(1, 1)
  call songwriter#tab#Lint()
Expect:
  e|--3--5--|

Given (unclosed last bars are closed and aligned with closed ones):
  e|--3--|--5----
  B|--1--|--7--|

Execute (unclosed last bars are closed and aligned with closed ones):
  call cursor(1, 1)
  call songwriter#tab#Lint()
Expect:
  e|--3--|--5--|
  B|--1--|--7--|

Given (whitespace after the final pipe is not a bar):
  e|--3--|   

Execute (whitespace after the final pipe is not a bar):
  call cursor(1, 1)
  call songwriter#tab#Lint()
Expect:
  e|--3--|

Given songwriter (a cursor on a note of an unclosed bar stays on it):
  e|----3--5--

Execute (a cursor on a note of an unclosed bar stays on it):
  call cursor(1, 10)
  call songwriter#tab#edit#LintAndFollow(songwriter#tab#model#Read())
  AssertEqual 8, col('.')
Expect songwriter:
  e|--3--5--|

Given (an empty last bar is deleted (1.4)):
  e|--3--|-----|
  B|--1--|---|

Execute (an empty last bar is deleted (1.4)):
  call cursor(1, 1)
  call songwriter#tab#Lint()
Expect:
  e|--3--|
  B|--1--|

Given (every empty bar at the end is deleted, so lint is idempotent (1.4)):
  e|--3--|--|--|----|

Execute (every empty bar at the end is deleted, so lint is idempotent (1.4)):
  call cursor(1, 1)
  call songwriter#tab#Lint()
Expect:
  e|--3--|

Given (empty bars before the last one are kept (1.4)):
  e|--3--|--|--5--|

Execute (empty bars before the last one are kept (1.4)):
  call cursor(1, 1)
  call songwriter#tab#Lint()
Expect:
  e|--3--|--|--5--|

Given (a bar with a note on any string is not empty (1.4)):
  e|--3--|-----|
  B|--1--|--7--|

Execute (a bar with a note on any string is not empty (1.4)):
  call cursor(1, 1)
  call songwriter#tab#Lint()
Expect:
  e|--3--|-----|
  B|--1--|--7--|

Given (a tab with only empty bars keeps one (1.4)):
  e|----|--|
  B|--|------|

Execute (a tab with only empty bars keeps one (1.4)):
  call cursor(1, 1)
  call songwriter#tab#Lint()
Expect:
  e|--|
  B|--|

Given songwriter (a cursor in a deleted last bar lands on the tab's last pipe (1.4)):
  e|--3--|-----|

Execute (a cursor in a deleted last bar lands on the tab's last pipe (1.4)):
  call cursor(1, 10)
  call songwriter#tab#edit#LintAndFollow(songwriter#tab#model#Read())
  AssertEqual 8, col('.')
Expect songwriter:
  e|--3--|

Given (aligns misaligned bar pipes across strings, trims to two dashes (1.1/1.2)):
  e|-----5-----|
  B|---0--0-----|
  G|----------|
  a lyric line

Execute (aligns misaligned bar pipes across strings, trims to two dashes (1.1/1.2)):
  call cursor(2, 1)
  call songwriter#tab#Lint()
Expect:
  e|----5---|
  B|--0--0--|
  G|--------|
  a lyric line

Given (a string with no notes in a bar aligns with the noted strings):
  e|--5--|
  B|-----------|

Execute (a string with no notes in a bar aligns with the noted strings):
  call cursor(1, 1)
  call songwriter#tab#Lint()
Expect:
  e|--5--|
  B|-----|

Given (trims leading and trailing dashes to exactly two (1.2)):
  e|------5-----|

Execute (trims leading and trailing dashes to exactly two (1.2)):
  call cursor(1, 1)
  call songwriter#tab#Lint()
Expect:
  e|--5--|

Given (preserves relative order of notes, does not collapse sequential notes):
  e|----5-|
  B|-0-|

Execute (preserves relative order of notes, does not collapse sequential notes):
  call cursor(1, 1)
  call songwriter#tab#Lint()
Expect:
  e|-----5--|
  B|--0-----|

Given (handles multiple bars):
  e|---5--|---0--|
  B|------|--1-|

Execute (handles multiple bars):
  call cursor(1, 1)
  call songwriter#tab#Lint()
Expect:
  e|--5--|---0--|
  B|-----|--1---|

" Test: a 2-digit number's second digit overlapping a later note on a
" different line is pushed right so that exactly 1 dash separates the
" numbers (spec 1.3)

Given:
  e|---12---|
  B|----1---|

Execute:
  call cursor(1, 1)
  call songwriter#tab#Lint()
Expect:
  e|--12----|
  B|-----1--|

" Test: two overlapping 2-digit numbers on different lines get pushed
" apart with 1 dash between them (spec 1.3)

Given:
  e|---12---|
  B|----13---|

Execute:
  call cursor(1, 1)
  call songwriter#tab#Lint()
Expect:
  e|--12-----|
  B|-----13--|

" Test: two 2-digit numbers starting on the same column are aligned and
" must NOT be split (spec 1.3, the "but not aligned" exception)

Given:
  e|---12---|
  B|---12---|

Execute:
  call cursor(1, 1)
  call songwriter#tab#Lint()
Expect:
  e|--12--|
  B|--12--|

" Test: a single-digit note that merely aligns with the first digit of a
" 2-digit number on another line is not pushed (spec 1.3: only the second
" digit may overlap)

Given:
  e|---12---|
  B|---1----|

Execute:
  call cursor(1, 1)
  call songwriter#tab#Lint()
Expect:
  e|--12--|
  B|--1---|

Given (cursor anywhere in the block lints the whole block; canonical tab is unchanged):
  e|-----------4--|--1-----------|--3-----------|--3-----------|
  B|--------1-----|-----2-----2--|--------------|--------4--1--|
  G|--3-----0--0--|-----1--0--0--|--1-----------|--------------|
  D|--------1-----|-----1--------|-----1--------|-----1--1-----|
  A|--4--3--------|--1-----1-----|-----3--3--3--|--------3--1--|
  E|--3-----------|--1-----------|-----1--------|-----3--4--4--|

Execute (cursor anywhere in the block lints the whole block; canonical tab is unchanged):
  call cursor(6, 1)
  call songwriter#tab#Lint()
Expect:
  e|-----------4--|--1-----------|--3-----------|--3-----------|
  B|--------1-----|-----2-----2--|--------------|--------4--1--|
  G|--3-----0--0--|-----1--0--0--|--1-----------|--------------|
  D|--------1-----|-----1--------|-----1--------|-----1--1-----|
  A|--4--3--------|--1-----1-----|-----3--3--3--|--------3--1--|
  E|--3-----------|--1-----------|-----1--------|-----3--4--4--|

Given songwriter (lint keeps playing techniques such as h, / and x):
  e|--5h7--x--|
  B|--3/5-----|

Execute (lint keeps playing techniques such as h, / and x):
  SongwriterLint
Expect:
  e|--5h7--x--|
  B|--3/5-----|

Given songwriter (lint aligns pipes and the notes around separators):
  e|-----5h7----|---|
  B|---3/5--|--12b14--|

Execute (lint aligns pipes and the notes around separators):
  SongwriterLint
Expect:
  e|----5h7--|---------|
  B|--3/5----|--12b14--|

